{"id":"thm:elementary-minimax-bracket","kind":"theorem","statement":"For every fixed \(0<\epsilon<1/2\), there are constants \(0<c_\epsilon\le C_\epsilon<\infty\) and \(\rho_\epsilon>0\) such that, uniformly for \(2\le d\le\rho_\epsilon n\log(en)\),
\[
 c_\epsilon\left\{\frac{\sqrt d}{n}+\frac d{n\log(en)}\right\}
 \le\mathfrak R_{n,d,\epsilon}
 \le\sup_{P\in\mathcal P_{d,\epsilon}}
 E_P\!\left[
  \left\{\widehat V_n^{\mathrm{DAT}}-V^\star(P)\right\}^2
